orms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion during the afternoons and evenings both\nWednesday and Thursday.","ends":"2026-08-27T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Weld, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Larimer, CO; Broomfield, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 26 at 3:55PM MDT until August 26 at 11:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n629 IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING\nAREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 13 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTH CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nLARIMER\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              BOULDER\nBROOMFIELD            DENVER                DOUGLAS\nJEFFERSON             MORGAN                WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, ARVADA, AURORA, BOULDER,\nBROOMFIELD, CASTLE ROCK, CENTENNIAL, DENVER,\nDENVER INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT, ELIZABETH, FORT COLLINS,\nFORT MORGAN, GREELEY, KIOWA, LAKEWOOD, LIMON, LONGMONT, LOVELAND,\nPARKER, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-26T23:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Boulder, CO; Broomfield, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Jefferson, CO; Larimer, CO; Lincoln, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.848b288ba106b48f16a6ef11a13265d46c58da15.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.848b288ba106b48f16a6ef11a13265d46c58da15.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T17:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 261740 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1140 AM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered afternoon/evening thunderstorms expected for theI-25 Corridor and plains. A few storms could become severe, with large hail and strong winds possible. - Thunderstorm coverage decreases Thursday and Friday with mainly isolated high-based showers/","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T20:23:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Thursday...Scattered thunderstorms will move across the urban corridor and eastern plains late this afternoon and early evening with heavy rain, hail, and strong winds. Warmer and drier air moves in for Thursday with isolated high-based showers/thunderstorms. Gusty outflow winds will accompany the showers/thunderstorms while any rainfall will be light. LONG TERM","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"ccr01","station_name":"Cherry Creek Reservoir","distance_km":4,"soil_temp_5cm_f":95.14,"soil_temp_15cm_f":85.06,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":109.33,"wind_speed_mph":10.12,"air_temp_f":80.1,"relative_humidity":0.386,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/ccr01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KAPA","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KAPA 262153Z 12007KT 10SM SCT070 BKN120 BKN220 29/10 A3027 RMK AO2 SLP177 OCNL LTGICCG DSNT SE-SW CB DSNT SE-SW MOV SE T02890100","temp_f":84,"wind_dir":120,"wind_kt":7,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"BKN","flight_category":"V